  "description": "BALMAE crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H105 Er4 O28,0.63(C7 H8). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.535-3.865 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.56-112.62°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Er4(μ3-OH)4(mmc)8]·1.5 toluene. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
